findings
  none. No relation has a half on a document past the declared window.

relations, by the creator each one declares
  Q4 keeps `created_by` on the relation type, so every row is a relation and never
  an edge instance. Two halves of one relation carry one value whatever wrote them.
  `captured` is the share of eligible documents that declared at least one half.
  author — no relation declares it
  scaffold — no relation declares it
  generator — no relation declares it
  hook — no relation declares it
  agent — no relation declares it
  import — no relation declares it
  6 of the 6 creators the taxonomy model declares have no relation in this taxonomy: author, scaffold, generator, hook, agent, import.
  A comparison against any of them has one arm over this corpus, and the missing
  arm is a property of the taxonomy rather than of the authoring. No number below
  stands in for one.

the governed scope, and what reaches it
  no anchor kind declares a governed scope, so the tree side of `governs` has no
  denominator here. `anchors.<kind>.scope` declares one.

